cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CAPRI-Python in your research, please cite it."
title: "CAPRI-Python: A Python reimplementation of the core CAPRI agricultural economic model"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "CAPRI-Python contributors"
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/capri-python"
abstract: >
  CAPRI-Python is an independent Python reimplementation of the core of the CAPRI
  model (Common Agricultural Policy Regionalised Impact): a regional supply side
  (Positive Mathematical Programming over EU NUTS-2 regions) linked to a global
  Armington market. It reproduces CAPRI's 2017 base-year prices exactly but is not
  validated against CAPRI's scenario magnitudes. It is not an official CAPRI product.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "CAPRI model"
    notes: "The original CAPRI model, developed by EuroCARE / Bonn University."
    url: "https://www.capri-model.org"
